Tenant config bleed. Put this in /workspace/tenantcfg.py:

BASE_CONFIG = {
    "features": {"beta": False, "export": True},
    "limits": {"rate": 100, "burst": 20},
    "theme": "light",
}

def config_for(tenant_overrides):
    cfg = BASE_CONFIG.copy()
    for section, values in tenant_overrides.items():
        if isinstance(values, dict):
            cfg[section].update(values)
        else:
            cfg[section] = values
    return cfg

Because .copy() is shallow, one tenant's overrides mutate BASE_CONFIG for everyone. Prove it in tests/test_tenantcfg.py before fixing: build config_for({"limits": {"rate": 5}}), then config_for({}) and assert the second still has rate 100; also assert BASE_CONFIG itself is unchanged after any call. Run pytest, see the bleed, then fix (deep copy or a recursive merge that never mutates inputs) and add a test that nested override dicts passed by the caller are not mutated either. Finish green.

